# band is wide [derived].
kind: baseline
question: how fast is the model's own llama.cpp fork on Raon-1-mini-preview Q4_K_M on one RTX 3090, beside the
  bloomery long tape?
term: decode tok/s of llama-server's K3 tape (Korean, n-predict 2048), -ngl 99 -fa on -c 262144, RTX 3090
unit: tok/s
predict: 60..180
condition: one lease, the box quiet, the 3090 alone, a fresh server, two discarded warm-ups, io pressure some
  avg10 under 5 before the tape, greedy; then llama-bench pp512 tg128 three repetitions
reason: the user asked how the model's own llama.cpp compares; the release post's comparison line needs it
  measured in the same session conditions
decide-in: write both engines' rows side by side in the report, no ratio claimed in the README
decide-below: under 60: read the offload and flash-attention lines of the server log before quoting it
decide-above: beyond 180: read the server log and the tape's text before quoting it
